{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++17 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++17 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <cmath>\n#include <array>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nusing i64 = long long;\n\nconstexpr int MOD = 1000000007;\n\nint safe_add(int a, int b) {\n    return (a + b) % MOD;\n}\n\nint safe_mul(int a, int b) {\n    return static_cast<i64>(a) * b % MOD;\n}\n\nint fast_pow(int base, int exp) {\n    int res = 1;\n    while (exp > 0) {\n        if (exp & 1) res = safe_mul(res, base);\n        base = safe_mul(base, base);\n        exp >>= 1;\n    }\n    return res;\n}\n\narray<int, 1000001> lookup;\n\nint discrete_log(int base, int modulus) {\n    fill(lookup.begin(), lookup.end(), -1);\n    int s = static_cast<int>(sqrt(modulus));\n    int cur = 1;\n    int inv_base = fast_pow(base, modulus - 2);\n    \n    for (int i = 0; i <= s; ++i) {\n        if (lookup[cur] == -1) lookup[cur] = i;\n        cur = safe_mul(cur, inv_base);\n        if (cur == 1) return i + 1;\n    }\n    \n    int step = fast_pow(base, s);\n    cur = step;\n    for (int j = 1; j <= s; ++j) {\n        if (lookup[cur] != -1) {\n            return s * j + lookup[cur];\n        }\n        cur = safe_mul(cur, step);\n    }\n    \n    return -1;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int p, k;\n    cin >> p >> k;\n    \n    if (k == 1) {\n        cout << fast_pow(p, p);\n    } else if (k == 0) {\n        cout << fast_pow(p, p - 1);\n    } else {\n        int d = discrete_log(k, p);\n        cout << fast_pow(p, (p - 1) / d);\n    }\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static final int MOD = 1000000007;\n    static int[] lookup = new int[1000001];\n\n    static int safe_add(int a, int b) {\n        return (a + b) % MOD;\n    }\n\n    static int safe_mul(int a, int b) {\n        return (int) (((long) a * b) % MOD);\n    }\n\n    static int fast_pow(int base, int exp) {\n        int res = 1;\n        while (exp > 0) {\n            if ((exp & 1) == 1) {\n                res = safe_mul(res, base);\n            }\n            base = safe_mul(base, base);\n            exp >>= 1;\n        }\n        return res;\n    }\n\n    static int discrete_log(int base, int modulus) {\n        Arrays.fill(lookup, -1);\n        int s = (int) Math.sqrt(modulus);\n        int cur = 1;\n        int inv_base = fast_pow(base, modulus - 2);\n        \n        for (int i = 0; i <= s; ++i) {\n            if (lookup[cur] == -1) {\n                lookup[cur] = i;\n            }\n            cur = safe_mul(cur, inv_base);\n            if (cur == 1) {\n                return i + 1;\n            }\n        }\n        \n        int step = fast_pow(base, s);\n        cur = step;\n        for (int j = 1; j <= s; ++j) {\n            if (lookup[cur] != -1) {\n                return s * j + lookup[cur];\n            }\n            cur = safe_mul(cur, step);\n        }\n        \n        return -1;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);\n      